Z||000000||fierohoho||06-20-2001||09:41 AM||||Now I know my way around engines, I've been working on my own Fiero's for years but I started looking in the search area and I find references to a DIS or distributorless ignition system. <P>Now it seems from what I've read that my 84 2.5l is a DIS system, but, I have a coil pack and distributor. <P>I'm having trouble with an occasional miss at idle and it is getting worse to where I now have an occasional backfire when accelerating after coasting, (automatic tranny.<P>Just replaced the plugs and O2 sensor and will get a new coil pack today, but where if I have it is the crank sensor? Ignition mudule?<P>Cation, I may have follow-up questions later, thanks.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||5
Z||000001||84Bill||06-20-2001||10:29 AM||||DIS Ignitions have just a coil and no distributer, I'd look into replacing the ignition module. All sorts of bad things can happen when they start to go and then POOF! your engine dies and won't run. Also look over the vaccume hoses for cracks and leaks at the fittings. It is a good thing just to replace them anyway, even if they are not bad it will give you peace of mind. Sensors and other electronics I would not bother with unless your ECM is throwing codes at you.||||reg||14
Z||000002||Steve Normington||06-20-2001||10:44 AM||||Only the 87 and 88 4-cyd engines have DIS.||||reg||1
Z||000003||elfiero||06-20-2001||12:47 PM||||After you left the other night I had an idea-<BR>you could try swapping the distributor from<BR>your other engine-do you still have it?OR<BR>you could go to that secret place we keep<BR>our extra stuff and get another.also try<BR>swapping the TBI unit,could'nt hurt!Email me<BR>and we can talk about it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierohoho||06-20-2001||09:52 PM||||elfiero you have mail<P>Thanks guys, I took er to the cities after I replaced the O2 sensor and plugs. <P>No more miss or back fire, combo of the bad plugs/O2 sensor? <P>Actually felt pretty snappy. <P>So I passed on the new coil but I will soon go for a new mudule, anyone have the GM part number? <P>I did re-check the thread in the archives, I misread the year for the DIS, oops. Thanks for the help. <P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
